# Pano Info — Copy Share Link & Add as Portfolio Buttons

**Date:** 2026-06-02
**Branch:** master
**Status:** Approved

## Overview

Add two action buttons to the Google Info card footer in the panorama info page (`/my-tours/:mid/edit/:pid`). The buttons give photographers a fast path to copy a pano's Google Maps share link and save it directly to their Google Street View portfolio — without navigating away from the pano info page.

## Affected File

`src/pages/Tour/Detail/Edit/Info.jsx`

## Placement

Both buttons are added to the `CardFooter` of the `panoramaInfoGoogle` card, alongside the existing **Update** button. This footer already uses `gap-2` flex layout and is wrapped in the `!tour?.archived` guard — no structural changes needed.

Button order (left to right):

1. **Update** (existing)
2. **Copy Share Link** (new)
3. **Add as Portfolio** (new, conditional)

## Button 1 — Copy Share Link

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Label | "Copy Share Link" |
| Icon | `fa-solid fa-copy` |
| Visibility | Shown when `panoramaInfoGoogle.share_link` is truthy |
| Action | `navigator.clipboard.writeText(panoramaInfoGoogle.share_link)` |
| Success feedback | `toast.success(t('t_panorama_tools.t_image_info.t_detail_table.t_copied_share_link'))` |
| Loading state | None (clipboard write is instant) |
| Style | `className="dark:bg-zinc-500"` — matches existing Update button |

## Button 2 — Add as Portfolio

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Label | "Add as Portfolio" |
| Icon | `fa-solid fa-plus` |
| Visibility | Shown when `state.profile.photographer !== null` AND `panoramaInfoGoogle.share_link` is truthy |
| Action | `POST /photographers/portfolio/save` |
| Request body | `{ title: panoramaInfo.panorama_name, value: panoramaInfoGoogle.share_link, type: 'google' }` |
| Loading state | Button spinner + disabled while request is in flight |
| Success feedback | `toastHook({ data: res })` |
| Error feedback | `toastHook({ data: err })` |
| Style | `color="primary"` to visually distinguish as an additive action |
| Post-save | No page refresh or local state update needed |

## Photographer Visibility Logic

```js
const photographer = useSelector((state) => state.profile.photographer);
```

`photographer` is `null` in Redux when the user has not applied to the photographer directory. Any non-null value (status 1, 2, or 3) means they have applied or been approved — the button is shown.

## API Hook5

```js
const [addAsPortfolio, { loading: loadingAddAsPortfolio }] = usePost({
  url: '/photographers/portfolio/save',
});
```

Same pattern as `clearCache`, `updatePanorama`, and other `usePost` instances already in Info.jsx.

## Localization Keys

| Key | Value (EN) |
|---|---|
| `t_panorama_tools.t_image_info.t_detail_table.t_copied_share_link` | "Share link copied!" |
| `t_panorama_tools.t_image_info.t_detail_table.t_button_add_portfolio` | "Add as Portfolio" |

These keys must be added to all active translation files.

## What Does NOT Change

- The existing small inline copy icon next to the share_link table row stays as-is
- No new components — changes are self-contained in Info.jsx
- No routing or Redux state changes
- No changes outside the `panoramaInfoGoogle` card
